.\" mount.filsys.1 - part of filsys 1.0.0
.TH MOUNT.FILSYS 1 "August 2026" "filsys 1.0.0" "File Format and Disk Utilities"
.SH NAME
mount.filsys \- mount a Research Unix filesystem image via FUSE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mount.filsys
.BI \-v " edition"
.RB [ \-o
.IR offset= N [, uid= N , gid= N ,...]]
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-d ]
.I image mountpoint
.br
.B mount.filsys
.BI \-v " edition"
.RB [ \-o
.IR offset= N ]
.BI \-c " image"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mount.filsys
mounts a Research Unix (V4 through 32V) filesystem image as a FUSE filesystem.
The on-disk edition is selected at run time with
.BR \-v :
4, 5, 6 (V6), 7 (V7), or 32 (32V, the little-endian VAX layout).
.PP
A disk image may hold several filesystems
.RI ( partitions ),
selected by a partition table that is compiled into the kernel, not stored on
the disk.  By default the filesystem at block 0 is mounted; the
.B offset=
option (a byte offset) mounts a filesystem that begins elsewhere in the file.
.PP
With
.BR \-c ,
the filesystem is opened read-only and its integrity is checked
.RB ( fsck.filsys (1))
instead of mounting it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-v " edition"
Filesystem edition: one of 4, 5, 6, 7, or 32.  Required.
.TP
.BI \-o " offset= N [, option ...]"
FUSE options.  The filsys-specific
.B offset=
is the byte offset of the filesystem within the image; the rest (uid, gid, and
so on) are passed through to FUSE.
.TP
.B \-r
Mount read-only.
.TP
.B \-f
Stay in the foreground.
.TP
.B \-d
Enable FUSE debugging.
.TP
.B \-c
Check the filesystem instead of mounting.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mount.filsys -v 7 rp06-0.disk /mnt/v7
mount.filsys -v 7 -o offset=9416704 rp06-0.disk /mnt/usr
mount.filsys -v 7 -c rp06-0.disk
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR findfs.filsys (1),
.BR mkfs.filsys (1),
.BR fsck.filsys (1),
.BR filsys (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for the filsys project.
